{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And YHWH came down in the cloud and spoke to him and took from the spirit that was upon him and placed it upon the seventy men, the elders.</b> The sage Rabbi Abraham, of blessed memory, wrote: our Sages said that Moses took from each tribe six, six, and they are seventy-two; and because the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him 'seventy men,' he left the two — and this is correct, end of his words." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> Moses took seventy-two slips and wrote 'elder' upon seventy of them and upon the two he wrote 'lot.' Whoever drew in his hand 'elder' — it was known that he was appointed; whoever drew in his hand 'lot' — it came to him from HaShem that he was not worthy of appointment. Eldad and Medad were in the camp and were men of great humility, and did not wish to take the crown and go to the Tent to draw the slips, even though they were worthy of it, as Scripture testified: והמה בכתובים — 'and they were among the inscribed,' that is, among the choicest of Israel, for they were of the Sanhedrin; and out of abundant humility they did not go out to the Tent. And this is what it says: וישארו שני אנשים במחנה — 'and two men remained in the camp' — for they were ashamed before the others. And by virtue of the trait of humility that was in them, they merited the holy spirit (ru'aḥ ha-kodesh); and concerning this it says ולא יצאו האהלה ויתנבאו במחנה — 'and they did not go out to the Tent and prophesied in the camp' — this explains that by virtue of their humility in not going out to the Tent, they merited that they prophesied in the camp itself. And we find an explicit verse that by virtue of humility a person merits the holy spirit, as it is written (Isaiah 61:1): ״ורוח ה' אלהים עלי יען משח ה' אותי לבשר ענוים״ — 'and the spirit of YHWH Elohim is upon me, because HaShem has anointed me to bring good tidings to the humble.' And by virtue of the humility that was in them they had a superiority over the elders, for the elders did not prophesy except until the morrow, as it says: ואל העם תאמר התקדשו למחר — 'and to the people you shall say: sanctify yourselves for tomorrow'; whereas these prophesied until the days of the Messiah, concerning the downfall of Gog and Magog, in the manner written in Ezekiel (38): ״כה אמר ה' האתה הוא אשר דברתי בימים קדמונים ביד עבדי נביאי ישראל הנבאים בימים ההם שנים להביא אותך עליהם״ — and our Sages, of blessed memory, interpreted: do not read שנים (years) but שנים (two). And furthermore, the elders' names were not specified whereas these had their names specified. And furthermore, the elders prophesied only from the spirit of Moses, whereas these prophesied from the spirit of the Holy One, blessed be He; this is what Moses said to Joshua: המקנא אתה לי ומי יתן כל עם ה' נביאים כי יתן ה' את רוחו עליהם — 'are you jealous for me? and would that all the people of HaShem were prophets, that HaShem would give His spirit upon them' — that is, just as He gives of His spirit upon these elders. And furthermore, the elders died in the wilderness and did not enter the land, whereas Eldad and Medad entered the land: Eldad is Elidad son of Chislon, and Medad is Kemuel son of Shiftan, who were chosen to apportion the land (Numbers 34:21). From this you learn that by virtue of humility they merited the holy spirit and had superiority over the elders. And what it says, <b>and it came to pass when the spirit rested upon them</b> — meaning from Moses, for thus it stated: ויאצל מן הרוח אשר עליו — 'and he took from the spirit that was upon him.' And what it says of Eldad and Medad, ותנח עליהם הרוח — 'and the spirit rested upon them' — meaning from the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>Know</b> that from this verse, וירד ה' בענן וידבר אליו, a great and holy Name is derived."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:44.015201907Z", 